{
  "format": "sfxgen/1",
  "name": "Big boom with debris",
  "description": "A fuel depot goes up some way off. The explosion is built the way film sound does it: a sharp, complete bang recorded 'small' (a crack, a drum-like thump and a burst of fire noise) is played back slowed down, so everything in it becomes slow, low and enormous: the crack stretches, the boom takes its time to fall, and the fire roars on. Then the debris comes down: lumps of rubble thudding and clacking, big pieces first. Last, a big broken slab of stone lands with a dull crash and clatters to rest in closing bounces.",
